c_double_complex,"] [293 2 "// c_float_complex, c_longdouble_complex): two parts in the type of 'd', 'f' and 'g', laid out as C's _Complex (in ci a"] [294 2 "// memory value, passed as a struct of its parts); the value set from PyComplex_AsCComplex's answer (asCComplex)"] [341 2 "// G: two long doubles of 16 bytes each (C's long double _Complex)"] [358 2 "// c: a single byte"] [362 2 "// u: a wchar_t (4 bytes on ci's target)"] [366 2 "// U: a wchar_t array as a str; s: a char array as bytes"] [369 2 "// z, Z, P, O: pointers"] [531 3 "// CPython stores the bytes object's own buffer and keeps the object (b_objects shows it); here its copy in"] [532 3 "// the world, kept as long as the bytes object is (bytesCopies)"] [627 1 "// bytesCopies are the world's copies of the bytes objects c_char_p values hold (one per object, for its life)."] [640 1 "// storeX87 writes x as a long double (x87's extended, its 6 padding bytes zero) at ptr."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[88 23] [384 28] [408 26] [436 20] [436 27] [457 20] [457 32] [494 20] [494 30] [631 24]] :go/trails [[190 52]]} (go/file "cfield.go" :imports [

